# Autbiz frontend — environment.
#
# Copy to .env.local for development. Never commit .env.local.

# The backend's origin. SERVER-SIDE ONLY, and read at BUILD time by
# next.config.ts (rules.md §21) — changing it needs a redeploy, not a restart.
#
# Set it for Production AND Preview. "Works in Production, broken in Preview"
# is this variable, every time.
#
# A trailing slash is stripped defensively; a pasted origin usually carries one
# and the doubled path 404s in a way that points nowhere near the cause.
BACKEND_ORIGIN=http://localhost:8000

# DO NOT ADD a public API URL variable (NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL or similar).
# It overrides the /api proxy and points the browser straight at the API host,
# re-introducing cross-origin, SameSite=None and preflight — undoing the entire
# same-origin design. This has already caused a production outage on a sibling
# project, where the value was not even a URL and every login posted to
# /8000/auth/login.
